  "boundary": "This plan establishes fail-closed Section 48 field-evidence collection controls for human, device, assistive-technology, performance, and energy groups. It reuses approved companion methods but never inherits their evidence automatically. Each candidate record must target one v1.3 lane, bind the frozen source and exact tooling/integration identity, include Section 48-specific observations, and survive separate governed review before it may satisfy an evidence group. CI, templates, synthetic fixtures, emulators, automation, or a companion-protocol pass cannot establish Section 48 evidence or any V1.7.1 lifecycle, consumer, deployment, publication, or production authority."
